<title>UK: Stadco joint venture to open auto parts factory.</title>
<headline>Stadco joint venture to open auto parts factory.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stadco Pressings, the automobile components unit of Britain's Hall Engineering (Holdings) Plc, said on Thursday that over 100 jobs will be created at a new automotive parts factory in Gloucestershire, south west England.</p>
<p>The project will be run by a new joint venture company between Stadco and Takao Europe, which is owned by Takao Kinzoku Kyogu Company Ltd, and will be called STE (Stadco Takao Europe).</p>
<p>The factory is due for completion in the autumn and will serve clients including Honda in Swindon, southern England.</p>
<p>Hall has a 65 percent interest in the joint venture.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
